# ── Chrome Extension ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# API keys are stored in chrome.storage.local and configured via the
# extension's options page — not through environment variables. A browser
# extension runs off the nanohype substrate, where the LLM policy permits a
# provider key only for the provider the intake brief names.
# This file exists for consistency across templates.
#
# During development, Vite reads from .env if present:
# VITE_DEFAULT_PROVIDER=anthropic
